.TH ZWHOIS 1 "October 2026" "zwhois 0.1.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zwhois \- WHOIS-style RDAP registration and optional DNS/hosting audit tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zwhois
.RI [ options ] " domain|hostname|IPv4|IPv6|ASnumber ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show available RDAP registration information, including independent registry and
registrar expiration dates, registration dates, registrar, status, and nameservers.
IP address and AS number arguments return network registration information instead.
Optional switches add live DNS, hosting network and reputation observations.
There are no third-party Python dependencies; DNS checks require the system
.B dig
command. The tool never crawls web pages or performs certificate health checks.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I target
A registered domain, full hostname, IPv4 address, IPv6 address, or AS number
(such as AS15169). Multiple targets are permitted. If none is given and standard
input is redirected, read one target per line. Comments starting with # are ignored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-mail
Look up MX hosts, their IP addresses, and RDAP network operators.
.TP
.B \-w, \-\-web
Look up A/AAAA/CNAME for the target and www-prefixed target, with RDAP IP allocation owners.
.TP
.B \-H, \-\-hosting
Combined web and mail infrastructure observations; does not perform security or blocklist checks.
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-subdomains
Check selected common subdomain records, not an exhaustive enumeration.
.TP
.B \-S, \-\-security
Print SPF/DMARC TXT content and configured DKIM selector TXT lookups. This is not
an SPF/DKIM policy verifier, and absent probed selectors do not prove no DKIM exists.
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-blocklists
Query configured IP-based DNSBLs for web and MX IPs. Some lists may restrict
querying and not support IPv6. Provider errors are not listings.
.TP
.B \-ns, \-\-nameservers
Independently check parent-zone NS referral and in-domain A/AAAA glue, compare
with child authoritative DNS, and test available nameserver IPv4/IPv6 endpoints
using UDP and TCP for SOA and NS checks. Does not require zone transfer (AXFR).
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-full
Perform all available optional checks.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-dialog
Interactive terminal interface using dialog (or whiptail), preserving current
target and selected test options when returning to the main menu.
.TP
.B \-\-config PATH
Read optional JSON settings from PATH, overriding ~/.config/zwhois/config.json.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show program version.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Detailed help and examples.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B zwhois example.com
Read registrar, registration/expiration dates, and registered nameservers.
.TP
.B zwhois secure.example.com
Fetch registered parent domain data, keeping the full hostname for optional DNS tests.
.TP
.B zwhois -H -ns example.com
Combined web/mail and delegation/glue/transport report.
.TP
.B zwhois -m -S -b example.com
Combine mail host, email TXT and reputation checks.
.TP
.B zwhois 8.8.8.8
IP address allocation lookup.
.TP
.B zwhois AS15169
Autonomous system registration lookup.
.TP
.B zwhois -d
Open interactive menu in a real terminal.
.TP
.B zwhois < domains.txt > audit.txt
Read newline-delimited targets from a file and save report to another file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/zwhois/config.json
User settings. A template is shipped under share/doc/zwhois/example.json.
.SH HOW GLUE CHECKS WORK
Parent DNS authority is consulted with recursion disabled, and referral authority
and additional sections are interpreted separately. Glue is not inferred from
normal recursive A/AAAA results. Missing AAAA glue is a warning, not automatically
a protocol violation. Checks can be inconclusive if servers are unreachable.
.SH EXPIRATION DATES
Registry Expires comes from the RDAP eventAction "expiration". Registrar Expires
comes from "registrar expiration", preferably obtained directly from the registrar's
RDAP service discovered using the IANA Registrar IDs directory and the registrar's
IANA ID. If direct retrieval is unavailable, a registrar expiration event in the
registry response can be used as a clearly identified fallback; otherwise the
registrar date is shown as Not provided. The two dates may differ after registry
auto-renewal. Differences over 60 seconds, or dates falling on different UTC
calendar days, generate a warning; small same-day rounding differences do not.
Both original timestamps are always displayed. Verify actual customer renewal
and payment dates with the registrar.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Public RDAP can redact fields or omit dates; registry expiration can differ from
registrar billing. Network registration owners may differ from hosting operators.
No exhaustive DKIM or subdomain discovery is possible using these DNS lookups.
DNSBLs require adherence to provider policies. The DNS checks do not perform
AXFR or guarantee reachability from every network.
